x 
x On the UI side:
x I'm going to mention some specific colors.  Make a common theme file (maybe json?) shared by
x both platforms that defines the colors, so we can iterate the theme in one place.
x 
x Add a 1x1 button to the right of the wide plate-selector
x called FLDR (we'll add icons later :v). When it's clicked, the plate is replaced with a scrollable
x grid of 2w3h-thumb thumbnail boxes (with 0.3 thumb gutters and margins). Each thumbnail represents a plate.
x 
x The box starts with a #303030 background (defined in the theme file). Then, if a thumbnail is available
x for the plate (preprocessor is working on those now, I'll have them in the index for you shortly),
x paint that thumbnail image to fill the rect. (It may have transparency, so some gray will peek through the
x edges. Then paint a rectangle at the bottom, full width, in a color to be specified, as a background for
x the label. Then paint the plate label over that color block.
x 
x Color assignments:
x 	csup, airport-diagram, takeoff-mins - blue 1a84d8
x 	approach - burnt orange b1591a
x 	departure - green 518b12
x 	STAR - magenta b93f8a
x On the grid, sort the plate thumbnails:  airport diagram, csup, to-mins, approach, departure, star

